      "content": "i just feel like the shame is permanent. no matter how much i talk or how much a counselor says it's just a feeling, it doesn't change the reality that i'm a disappointment. sometimes i think the only way to actually stop the damage is to just... stop being a part of it. like, if i wasn't here, the disappointment would just end. they wouldn't have to watch me fail anymore. it almost feels like the only way to protect them is to just not be a burden to them anymore.",
